  "id": "active-dead-hang",
  "name": "Active Dead Hang",
  "definition": "A strict bilateral timed hang from a horizontal pull-up bar using a shoulder-width closed pronated grip, unsupported feet, fully extended elbows, no deliberate swing, and the shoulder blades held down so the shoulders remain away from the ears. Gravity tends to elevate the scapulae and open the fingers; scapula.elevation and hand.fingerExtension are resisted tendencies, not dynamic repetitions. Army and CrossFit standards directly establish the bar, grip, straight-arm suspension, and active shoulder boundary. Lower-trapezius, grip, and support-chain roles are conservative anatomy-and-mechanics inferences rather than exact-fixture rankings. Passive Dead Hang, Scapular Pull-Up, flexed-arm holds, Pull-Ups, climbing-edge hangs, weighted hangs, swinging, and foot-assisted hangs remain outside this contract.",
